This means that the Tribunal should consider and decide with reference to the evidence:
(i) whether the disablement is permanent or temporary;
Smt. Roshan Aara vs Pushkar Hira on 25 August, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/191802696/
5 (ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is permanent total disablement or permanent partial disablement;
(iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with reference to any specific limb,
then the effect of such disablement of the limb on the functioning of the entire body,that is, the permanent disability suffered by the person.
